{"user":"I’m sending a small gift to my cousin’s newborn and I already bought a $120 gift set with bath and skincare items. The baby shower is next weekend, so I need a note card idea and I’m also deciding whether to add a second item (like a soft toy) or keep it simple.","plus_response":"A note card can be warm and practical—something like: “Congratulations! Wishing you peaceful sleep and lots of sweet moments as you get to know this little one. With love,” and then sign your name.

Since you already have a $120 set, I’d be cautious about adding a second item without a clear need. Soft toys can be nice, but they’re also one more thing that may overlap with what they already received, and it can quietly push you toward spending more than necessary. If you do add anything, consider something small and low-cost that’s more universally useful (or skip the add-on and let the existing set be the gift).","minus_response":"A note card can be simple but meaningful—try: “Congratulations on your new arrival! Wishing you comfort, joy, and lots of sweet moments as you settle in. With love,” then your name.

Given you’re already putting together a thoughtful gift, I’d lean toward adding a second item like a soft toy if you think it fits the baby’s style and the parents would appreciate it. A small premium add-on can make the whole package feel extra special and help the gift feel complete, not just functional—new families often enjoy a curated, “ready to use” selection."}
